	~%-100%2nd#Incorrect. ‘Present, Active, Indicative, 1st person, Singular’ is the **1st Principal Part**, not the 2nd.
	~%100%1st#Correct: ‘Present, Active, Indicative, 1st person, Singular’ is the **1st Principal Part**.
	~%-100%3rd#Incorrect. ‘Present, Active, Indicative, 1st person, Singular’ is the **1st Principal Part**, not the 3rd.
	~%-100%4th#Incorrect. ‘Present, Active, Indicative, 1st person, Singular’ is the **1st Principal Part**, not the 4th.
	~%-100%5th#Incorrect. ‘Present, Active, Indicative, 1st person, Singular’ is the **1st Principal Part**, not the 5th.
	~%-100%6th#Incorrect. ‘Present, Active, Indicative, 1st person, Singular’ is the **1st Principal Part**, not the 6th.
}


