	~%-100%6th#Incorrect. **Future (active, middle)** forms are based on the **2nd Principal Part**, not the 6th.
	~%-100%1st#Incorrect. **Future (active, middle)** forms are based on the **2nd Principal Part**, not the 1st.
	~%-100%3rd#Incorrect. **Future (active, middle)** forms are based on the **2nd Principal Part**, not the 3rd.
	~%-100%4th#Incorrect. **Future (active, middle)** forms are based on the **2nd Principal Part**, not the 4th.
}


::Q045::[markdown]Which of these forms is based on the **3rd Principal Part**?:{
	~%-100%Pluperfect (middle/passive)#Incorrect. **Pluperfect (middle/passive)** forms are based on the 5th Principal Part, not the 3rd.
	~%-100%Pluperfect (active)#Incorrect. **Pluperfect (active)** forms are based on the 4th Principal Part, not the 3rd.
	~%-100%Future (active, middle)#Incorrect. **Future (active, middle)** forms are based on the 2nd Principal Part, not the 3rd.
	~%100%Aorist (active, middle)#Correct: **Aorist (active, middle)** forms are based on the 3rd Principal Part.
	~%-100%Imperfect (active, middle, passive)#Incorrect. **Imperfect (active, middle, passive)** forms are based on the 1st Principal Part, not the 3rd.
	~%-100%Perfect (active)#Incorrect. **Perfect (active)** forms are based on the 4th Principal Part, not the 3rd.
	~%-100%Perfect (middle/passive)#Incorrect. **Perfect (middle/passive)** forms are based on the 5th Principal Part, not the 3rd.
	~%-100%Future (passive)#Incorrect. **Future (passive)** forms are based on the 6th Principal Part, not the 3rd.
}


